
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261029~sparky9~0 (2026-10-29)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Added German, Japanese, Korean, Simplified Chinese and Traditional Chinese strings

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261008.2~sparky9~0 (2026-10-08)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * The build no longer stops at dh_shlibdeps on computers whose /etc/ld.so.conf.d lists another folder before the distribution's (CUDA's OpenCL, PipeWire's JACK): dpkg-shlibdeps now looks in the distribution's own library folders first, as on a clean build machine (found on the first host build, 2026-10-08)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261008.1~sparky9~0 (2026-10-08)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * First version: sparky-stereo-ffmpeg-fdk rebuilds the edition's FFmpeg (ffmpeg-dmo, build profile pkg.ffmpeg-dmo.fdk) on the user's own computer with Fraunhofer's AAC encoder
  * Says plainly before anything is built that the result is for that computer only (FFmpeg's LICENSE.md), and how long the build takes
  * Installs the result as VERSION+fdkN, kept by apt through a pin the build writes (the exact version of each installed package, with its architecture, at 1002); the 32-bit libraries are the edition's own, relabelled to the same version (Multi-Arch: same)
  * An apt hook rebuilds by itself, in the background, when the edition updates FFmpeg; --status, --remove (back to the edition's FFmpeg)
